# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env. In Vercel: Settings → Environment Variables
#
# Supabase: Connect → Connection string → "Transaction pooler" (port 6543)
# Copy the WHOLE string from Supabase, and only replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with your database password.
# Don't copy the example below: the host (aws-0-... or aws-1-..., and the region) is different for every project.
# A wrong host gives: "tenant/user postgres.xxxx not found"
#
# It looks something like this:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-<n>-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
